}}{{Use dmy dates|date=April 2022}}The '''2022 Sunderland City Council election''' took place on 5 May 2022 to elect members of [[Sunderland City Council]]. This is on the same day as [[2022 United Kingdom local elections|other elections across the United Kingdom]].

==Background==
24 of the 75 seats will be up for election<ref>{{cite web |title=Election timetable in England |url=https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/election-timetable-in-england/election-timetable-in-england#metropolitan-districts |access-date=9 April 2022 |website=GOV.UK |language=en}}</ref> All 25 wards were originally due to elect councillors, however the election in Copt Hill ward was postponed following the death of the city's only UKIP candidate.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Graham |first=Hannah |date=2022-04-21 |title=Vote on hold as 'dedicated' council candidate dies during campaign |url=https://www.chroniclelive.co.uk/news/north-east-news/copt-hill-sunderland-ukip-election-23743821 |access-date=2022-05-06 |website=ChronicleLive |language=en}}</ref> 

Since the first election in [[1973 Sunderland Metropolitan Borough Council election|1973]], Sunderland has been a strongly [[Labour Party (UK)|Labour]] council, which consistently achieves over 60% control of the council.<ref>{{cite web |title=Sunderland City Council Election Results 1973-2012 |url=http://www.electionscentre.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2015/06/Sunderland-1973-2012.pdf |website=Elections Centre |access-date=15 April 2022}}</ref> [[2021 Sunderland City Council election|2021]] represented the worst year for Labour in terms of seats; the party lost 9 with 39.2% of the vote.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Graham |first1=Hannah |title=Tories hope for Labour loss in Sunderland council elections |url=https://www.chroniclelive.co.uk/news/north-east-news/sunderland-local-election-results-prediction-23624285 |access-date=15 April 2022 |work=ChronicleLive |date=8 April 2022 |language=en}}</ref> The [[Conservative Party (UK)|Conservatives]] gained 6 with 34.8%, the [[Liberal Democrats (UK)|Liberal Democrats]] gained 4 with 15.4%, [[UK Independence Party|UKIP]] did not make any further gains with 4.5%, and the [[Green Party of England and Wales|Green Party]] lost representation on the council with 5.2%.

There had been speculation ahead of the election that the Labour Party could lose overall control of Sunderland City Council for the first time in its history. 

The seats up for election this year were last elected in [[2018 Sunderland City Council election|2018]]. In that election, Labour won 61 seats (a net loss of 4 seats). The Conservatives gained 2 seats while the Liberal Democrats gained 3 seats on the Council. 1 independent councillor lost their seat.

== Election results ==
After the election, the Labour Party maintained control of the Council. Labour's majority was reduced to 4, having lost 1 seat to the Liberal Democrats in Doxford Ward. In Fulwell, the Conservatives also lost a seat to the Liberal Democrats with a swing of 15%<ref>{{Cite web |title='Complacent' Labour and Conservatives handed Lib Dems gains in Sunderland local elections |url=https://www.sunderlandecho.com/news/politics/complacent-labour-and-conservatives-handed-lib-dems-gains-in-sunderland-local-elections-3684026 |access-date=2022-05-07 |website=www.sunderlandecho.com |language=en}}</ref>

The results defied media speculation that [[Labour Party (UK)|Labour]] would continue to haemorrhage seats like in [[2021 Sunderland City Council election|2021]] and [[2019 Sunderland City Council election|2019]]. Labour leader Graeme Miller commented that "It was a good night" for his party because they "stopped the rot". Conservative Group leader Anthony Mullen, blamed his party's poor performance on the [[Partygate]] Scandal, after the Conservatives failed to gain seats in Washington South, Ryhope, St Anne's or Silksworth. Liberal Democrat leader Niall Hodson said his party's gains from both Labour and the Conservatives were a result of “good candidates working hard for a long period of time”.<ref>{{cite web | url=https://www.sunderlandecho.com/news/politics/complacent-labour-and-conservatives-handed-lib-dems-gains-in-sunderland-local-elections-3684026 | title='Complacent' Labour and Conservatives handed Lib Dems gains in Sunderland local elections }}</ref>
